{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794481625,"nonce":"LYkMdbbnm9PMSEtIwVOAU9liwQE=","message":"First version built on 2026-11-12, for C (not C++), as `hxn import` and the new crate `hxn-c`.\n\nWhat it does: clang's JSON AST (`clang -Xclang -ast-dump=json -fparse-all-comments`) -\u003e `hxn_c::Api` -\u003e WebIDL (`\u003cname\u003e.webidl`, edited and committed) -\u003e `src/bindings.rs` (generated on every `hxn build`/`hxn check` from `[package.metadata.hxn] webidl`) -\u003e the usual hxn pipeline. The generated crate also works as a plain Rust crate.\n\nDecisions:\n- clang's JSON dump instead of libclang or bindgen: no native library to link, and `serde_json` is already a dependency. clang has to be installed. clang writes a location's `file` only when it changes, so the reader tracks the current file across nodes.\n- A small parser of its own for the WebIDL subset instead of walking weedle2's AST: line-numbered errors for hand edits, and much less code. weedle2 is a dev-dependency that checks the importer's output is valid WebIDL.\n- x-idl reads standard browser IDL and has no C dialect, so there was nothing to align with. The dialect is plain WebIDL plus `HxnC`, `HxnFree`, `HxnStatus`, `HxnReturns`, `HxnRef`, `HxnEnum` (documented in `crates/hxn-c/src/idl.rs`).\n- C enums are `[HxnEnum] interface X { const long V = n; }` because a WebIDL `enum` has string values.\n- Objects take `\u0026mut self` in every method and are only `Send`: a C library is not assumed to be thread-safe, and hxn's handle needs `Sync` for `\u0026self`.\n- Returned object pointers are taken as owned. A function that returns a borrowed pointer to an object would be freed twice; remove it from the WebIDL or wrap it by hand.\n\nFixture: `tests/cimport` (tally.h/c, the importer's exact output `imported.webidl`, the edited `tally.webidl` with `[HxnStatus]` on `add`, Main.hx, expected.txt).\n\nRun on 2026-11-12, macOS: `tests/cimport/run.sh` on Ash (hybrid, JIT, interpreter), hxcpp, CPPIA and Emscripten: all pass. `cargo test -p hxn-c` (5 tests). Not run: stock HashLink on the NUC (no clang there), Windows and Linux (added to CI), iOS and Android.\n\n`hxn build cpp --wasm` now sets `CC_`/`AR_wasm32_unknown_emscripten` to emcc/emar unless already set: without that the `cc` crate compiled C with the system clang and found no libc headers.\n\nNot built yet:\n- Callbacks (function pointer plus `void *` user data).\n- Out-parameters, arrays other than a bytes pointer with a `size_t` length, struct fields other than booleans and numbers, nullable text parameters.\n- Borrowed (non-owned) returned objects; thread-safe objects (`\u0026self` and `Sync`).\n- `hl --wasm`: C for wasm32-wasip1 needs the WASI SDK.\n- C++: bound through a C API over it for now.\n- Unions, `#define` constants, variadic functions (listed as not imported).","files":null}]}